    "https://blackburn.edu/jobs/assistant-coach-mens-wrestling/": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Coach - Men’s Wrestling - Blackburn College Skip to content Visit Apply Info Give Visit Apply Info Give Search Work Colleges I am a… A Future Student An Accepted Student A Current Student A Faculty or Staff Member A Family Member or Guardian An Alumnus/Alumna A High School Counselor I am a… A Future Student An Accepted Student A Current Student A Faculty or Staff Member A Family Member or Guardian An Alumnus/Alumna A High School Counselor Popular Pages News Homecoming & Family Weekend Employment Opportunities Library Resources Campus Map Student Success Center Blackburn Ranked #1 in Illinois Blackburn College has earned top honors in Washington Monthly’s 2025 college guide, ranking as the #1 bachelor’s college in Illinois and 20th in the nation, reflecting the College’s historic mission to provide access and deliver transformative educational experiences for students from all economic and social backgrounds. Learn more about our rankings About About Blackburn College Administrative Offices Community Leadership Mission & Vision Our History Consumer Information and Student Right-to-Know Sustainability Work Program About the Work Program Student Leadership Student Job Areas Outcomes Academics Academics at Blackburn Majors & Academic Programs Online Professional Education Blackburn & Beyond Academic Calendar Course Catalog Center for Teaching & Learning Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Blackburn Tuition & Costs Financial Aid Schedule a Visit Transfer Students International Students Readmission Life on Campus About Life on Campus Student Life Residence Life Student Stories Arts & Creative Expression Athletics & Intramurals Resources for Students News Events Directory Athletics Giving Alumni Visit Apply Info Give Home / Jobs / Assistant Coach – Men’s Wrestling Staff Assistant Coach – Men’s Wrestling Athletics Share This Job Part-Time, 10-Month Appointment Department: Athletics Reports To: Head Men’s Wrestling Coach Location: Blackburn College – Carlinville, IL Position Overview: Blackburn College, a Division III member of the NCAA and the St. Louis Intercollegiate Athletic Conference (SLIAC), invites applications for the position of Assistant Men’s Wrestling Coach. This is a part-time, 10-month position designed to support the continued development of a competitive and student-centered program. The Assistant Coach will play an integral role in team preparation, recruiting, academic support, and day-to-day operations of the program. We are looking for an individual who demonstrates strong leadership, a passion for mentorship, and a commitment to the mission of Division III athletics and the values of Blackburn College. Key Responsibilities: Assist with all aspects of a competitive NCAA Division III men’s wrestling program. Attend and actively participate in practices, games, and team travel. Support the recruitment of student-athletes who are a strong fit for Blackburn academically and athletically. Contribute to practice planning and game-day strategy. Promote the academic and personal development of student-athletes. Support the head coach in administrative tasks, including inventory management, scheduling, and compliance. Participate in departmental and team fundraising activities. Attend athletic department meetings and staff development opportunities. Positively represent the college in campus, conference, and community settings. Qualifications: Previous experience as a coach or athlete at the high school, collegiate, or professional level. Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills. Ability to work collaboratively with coaches, support staff, and campus departments. A genuine interest in mentoring student-athletes and contributing to their overall college experience. Must meet the physical requirements of the position The salary range is $8,000-$15,000. To Apply: Blackburn College features a robust benefits package. For additional information, please visit https://blackburn.edu/about/administrative-offices/human-resources/ and click on the Employee Benefits Summary Tab. Blackburn College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and seeks to build an inclusive community that can engage the interests of a diverse population. We are committed to fostering, cultivating, and sustaining a culture that reflects the diversity of our country, and as such we particularly encourage applications from members of underrepresented groups such as women, people of color, LGBTQ+, veterans, and those with disabilities. Interested candidates should submit their resume, cover letter including a diversity statement describing what diversity means to you and why it is important, the names/addresses/phone numbers of three current, and professional references to: Human Resources, Blackburn College, 700 College Ave., Ludlum 110, Carlinville, IL 62626 or email [email protected] . Employment-based immigration sponsorship is not offered for this position. Phone calls or walk-ins not accepted. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position has been filled. WHERE LEADERS RISE 700 College Avenue Carlinville, IL 62626 800.233.3550 Info Visit Apply About Academics Admissions & Aid Life on Campus Work Program Give News Events Administrative Offices Directory Employment Opportunities Consumer Information Reporting Options Title IX at Blackburn College Library Resources © 2026 Blackburn College. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Sitemap"
    },
    "https://blackburn.edu/jobs/online-program-recruiting-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Online Program Recruiting Coordinator",
      "description": "Online Program Recruiting Coordinator - Blackburn College Skip to content Visit Apply Info Give Visit Apply Info Give Search Work Colleges I am a… A Future Student An Accepted Student A Current Student A Faculty or Staff Member A Family Member or Guardian An Alumnus/Alumna A High School Counselor I am a… A Future Student An Accepted Student A Current Student A Faculty or Staff Member A Family Member or Guardian An Alumnus/Alumna A High School Counselor Popular Pages News Homecoming & Family Weekend Employment Opportunities Library Resources Campus Map Student Success Center Blackburn Ranked #1 in Illinois Blackburn College has earned top honors in Washington Monthly’s 2025 college guide, ranking as the #1 bachelor’s college in Illinois and 20th in the nation, reflecting the College’s historic mission to provide access and deliver transformative educational experiences for students from all economic and social backgrounds. Learn more about our rankings About About Blackburn College Administrative Offices Community Leadership Mission & Vision Our History Consumer Information and Student Right-to-Know Sustainability Work Program About the Work Program Student Leadership Student Job Areas Outcomes Academics Academics at Blackburn Majors & Academic Programs Online Professional Education Blackburn & Beyond Academic Calendar Course Catalog Center for Teaching & Learning Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Blackburn Tuition & Costs Financial Aid Schedule a Visit Transfer Students International Students Readmission Life on Campus About Life on Campus Student Life Residence Life Student Stories Arts & Creative Expression Athletics & Intramurals Resources for Students News Events Directory Athletics Giving Alumni Visit Apply Info Give Home / Jobs / Online Program Recruiting Coordinator Staff Online Program Recruiting Coordinator Admissions Share This Job Apply Now Full-Time Help Shape the Future of Online Education Are you passionate about helping students achieve their educational goals? Blackburn College is seeking an enthusiastic and relationship-driven Online Program Recruiting Coordinator to help grow our innovative online education programs, including Early Childhood Education and Teacher Licensure. In this role, you’ll be more than a recruiter—you’ll be a guide, mentor, and advocate for prospective students as they take the next step in their educational journey. If you enjoy building relationships, solving problems, and making a meaningful impact, we’d love to hear from you. What You’ll Do Recruit and engage prospective students interested in Blackburn’s online education programs. Guide students through the admissions process, from initial inquiry to enrollment. Build meaningful relationships through phone, email, Zoom, and in-person communication. Assist students with admissions requirements, financial aid resources, and enrollment steps. Partner with the Registrar, Financial Aid, Business Office, and Academic Departments to create a seamless student experience. Represent Blackburn College at college fairs, community events, and recruitment activities. Develop partnerships with community colleges, particularly Early Childhood Associate Degree programs. Support enrollment, retention, and student success initiatives for Blackburn’s growing online programs. What You’ll Bring Bachelor’s degree required. Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills. A passion for helping students succeed. Strong organization, time management, and attention to detail. Ability to work independently while collaborating across campus. Comfort using Microsoft Office and other technology tools. Knowledge of financial aid processes is preferred. Valid driver’s license and ability to travel, including occasional evenings and weekends. Why Blackburn College? At Blackburn College, you’ll join a close-knit campus community dedicated to student success, innovation, and personalized education. You’ll have the opportunity to make a direct impact on students’ lives while helping expand access to quality online education. If you’re looking for a career where relationship-building, creativity, and purpose come together, we’d love to meet you. Apply today and help future students find their path at Blackburn College. Blackburn College features a robust benefits package. For additional information, please visit https://blackburn.edu/about/administrative-offices/human-resources/ and click on the Employee Benefits Summary Tab. Blackburn College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and seeks to build an inclusive community that can engage the interests of a diverse population. We are committed to fostering, cultivating, and sustaining a culture that reflects the diversity of our country, and as such we particularly encourage applications from members of underrepresented groups such as women, people of color, LGBTQ+, veterans, and those with disabilities. Interested candidates should submit their resume, cover letter including a diversity statement describing what diversity means to you and why it is important, the names/addresses/phone numbers of three current, and professional references to: Human Resources, Blackburn College, 700 College Ave., Ludlum 110, Carlinville, IL 62626 or email [email protected] . Employment-based immigration sponsorship is not offered for this position. Phone calls or walk-ins not accepted. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position has been filled. Compensation: $44,000.00 – $48,000.00 per year Blackburn College provides a rigorous and affordable liberal arts education integrated with a distinctive student-managed Work Program, preparing graduates for careers, community engagement, and lifelong learning while fostering critical thinking, leadership, diversity and inclusion, service, shared governance, and moral responsibility within a community that unites work, learning, and scholarship. Apply Now WHERE LEADERS RISE 700 College Avenue Carlinville, IL 62626 800.233.3550 Info Visit Apply About Academics Admissions & Aid Life on Campus Work Program Give News Events Administrative Offices Directory Employment Opportunities Consumer Information Reporting Options Title IX at Blackburn College Library Resources © 2026 Blackburn College. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Sitemap"
    },
