      "description": "Part-time Bus Driver - Blackburn College Skip to content Visit Apply Info Give Visit Apply Info Give Search Work Colleges I am a… A Future Student An Accepted Student A Current Student A Faculty or Staff Member A Family Member or Guardian An Alumnus/Alumna A High School Counselor I am a… A Future Student An Accepted Student A Current Student A Faculty or Staff Member A Family Member or Guardian An Alumnus/Alumna A High School Counselor Popular Pages News Homecoming & Family Weekend Employment Opportunities Library Resources Campus Map Student Success Center Blackburn Ranked #1 in Illinois Blackburn College has earned top honors in Washington Monthly’s 2025 college guide, ranking as the #1 bachelor’s college in Illinois and 20th in the nation, reflecting the College’s historic mission to provide access and deliver transformative educational experiences for students from all economic and social backgrounds. Learn more about our rankings About About Blackburn College Administrative Offices Community Leadership Mission & Vision Our History Consumer Information and Student Right-to-Know Sustainability Work Program About the Work Program Student Leadership Student Job Areas Outcomes Academics Academics at Blackburn Majors & Academic Programs Online Professional Education Blackburn & Beyond Academic Calendar Course Catalog Center for Teaching & Learning Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid at Blackburn Tuition & Costs Financial Aid Schedule a Visit Transfer Students International Students Readmission Life on Campus About Life on Campus Student Life Residence Life Student Stories Arts & Creative Expression Athletics & Intramurals Resources for Students News Events Directory Athletics Giving Alumni Visit Apply Info Give Home / Jobs / Part-time Bus Driver Staff Part-time Bus Driver Physical Plant Department Share This Job Blackburn College, a unique liberal arts college with a student-managed work program, invites applications for a part-time bus driver.  Tasks include transporting college students, faculty, and staff to college related events.  Some travel may require an overnight stay and/or travelling out of state.  Applicants must be available for daytime and evening travel to include weekends.  Requires appropriate driver’s license certifications to operate a 25 and 46 passenger bus.   Blackburn College seeks to build an inclusive community that can engage the interests of a diverse population. The payrate for this position is $23.00 per hour. We are committed to fostering, cultivating, and sustaining a culture that reflects the diversity of our country, and as such we particularly encourage applications from members of underrepresented groups such as women, people of color, LGBTQ+, veterans, and those with disabilities. Send resume, cover letter, the names/addresses/phone numbers of three current and professional references to: Human Resources, Blackburn College, 700 College Ave., Ludlum 110, Carlinville, IL  62626 or email [email protected] . Employment-based immigration sponsorship is not offered for this position.  Phone calls or walk-ins not accepted. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled.  EOE WHERE LEADERS RISE 700 College Avenue Carlinville, IL 62626 800.233.3550 Info Visit Apply About Academics Admissions & Aid Life on Campus Work Program Give News Events Administrative Offices Directory Employment Opportunities Consumer Information Reporting Options Title IX at Blackburn College Library Resources © 2026 Blackburn College. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Sitemap"
